  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Partnership Dominoes. 4p, 7 each. Line domino. Pass when blocked. 100 target.',
    Player: 'Partnership Dominoes: 4 players, partners opposite. 7 tiles each. Double-six leads first. Match ends, add to line. Block means lower pips wins. 100 to win match.',
    objective: 'Be first team to 100 points (or agreed target). Score by going out or by having fewer pips when blocked.',
    gameplay: "1. Start: In the first hand the holder of the double-six tile leads. Later hands use rotation or the previous winner leads, depending on variant. 2. Play: Add tiles to the line; touching ends must match. Doubles are placed at right angles. Must play if possible; otherwise pass (knock). 3. End: When a player empties their hand the team wins the deal. If blocked (four passes), the team with fewer pips wins. 4. Score: Winners score the losers' unplayed pip total, or all unplayed pips per variant.",
